title: "The Hussite Beginning: A Documentary Apparatus, 1409–1420"
message: "If you use this apparatus, please cite it as below — and cite the printed source for any passage you quote."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fassbender
    given-names: Pantaleon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6683-3617"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pantaleonfassbender-coder/The-Hussite-Beginning"
url: "https://the-hussite-beginning.netlify.app/"
abstract: >-
  A documentary apparatus for the beginning of the Hussite revolution,
  1409-1420, built from public-domain editions with the original (Latin,
  Czech, German) beside a working English translation, every excerpt read
  against the page images: the Decree of Kutna Hora and the quarrel over it
  (Palacky, Documenta, 1869); Peter of Mladonovice's account of the trial
  and death of Hus; Hus's letters from Constance (Palacky 1869, with the
  English of Workman and Pope 1904); Sigismund's revocation of the safe
  conducts, the Bohemian lords' petition and the council's letter to
  Bohemia (1415); the council's decrees (Mansi XXVII, 1784); Hus's De
  ecclesia in Schaff's English (1915); Ulrich Richental's chronicle (Buck
  1882); the protest of the Bohemian lords under 452 seals (1415); Poggio
  Bracciolini on the trial of Jerome of Prague (1416); and Laurence of
  Brezova's chronicle from Mount Tabor to Sigismund's coronation (Fontes
  rerum Bohemicarum V, 1893). With a timeline, a Compare page, ten plates,
  and an explicit list of what is not carried and why. Companion game:
  Salvus conductus. Companion site: The Hussite Field Armies.
keywords:
